  "title": "osf review run: lens-driven agent review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds `osf review run`, a new review pipeline that selects review lenses for a change, assembles a redacted context prompt, drives installed coding agents headless as reviewers, verifies their quoted findings against the files, reduces the answers to a per-lens and whole-review verdict, and journals every answer and the decision. It also adds the `[agents]`/`[review]` configuration tables, a shipped lens catalogue, a `scan-secret` rule, suppression ownership tracking, and a base-branch GitHub workflow that runs the review as the gate.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
